  "fields": [
    {
      "entryId": "dan-7-9",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Daniel sees thrones set in place; the Ancient of Days takes His seat; the court sits in judgment and books are opened. Jesus, Paul, and Revelation all place judgment in God's court before the final kingdom. Textual proof: Dan 7:9-10 is a heavenly judgment scene; Dan 7:22 says judgment was given to the saints of the Most High — i.e., a judicial verdict precedes their possession of the kingdom.",
      "density": 3.6107,
      "words": 69,
      "sentences": 3,
      "maxSentenceWords": 33,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": [
          "Daniel 7:9",
          "Daniel 7:22"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-8-14",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "An holy one answers: unto two thousand and three hundred days; then shall the sanctuary be made right. Hebrews shows the earthly sanctuary as pattern of the heavenly (Heb 8:1-2; 9:23-24). Leviticus 16 describes the annual cleansing of the sanctuary by blood. Textual proof: Daniel's time prophecy ends at a sanctuary event; Hebrews locates Christ's ministry in the true tabernacle; Leviticus defines what \"cleansed/right\" means in priestly context — removal of accumulated sin from the sanctuary.",
      "density": 3.1571,
      "words": 76,
      "sentences": 5,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": [
          "Hebrews 8:1"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-7-25",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The little power speaks against the Most High, wears out the saints, and holds sway for a time, times, and a dividing of time. First principle: prophetic time is bounded — the wear-out has a stopwatch on it.",
      "density": 2.3214,
      "words": 38,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 24,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-7-22",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The judgment came, and the saints of the Most High possessed the kingdom. Textual proof: heavenly court (v9-10) issues a verdict, then the saints receive dominion. Paul writes that the saints shall judge the world and even angels (1 Cor 6:2-3). Revelation 20:4 shows thrones and judgment given to those who reign with Christ.",
      "density": 2.2071,
      "words": 54,
      "sentences": 4,
      "maxSentenceWords": 15,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": [
          "1 Corinthians 6:2",
          "Revelation 20:4"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-7-27",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Dominion under the whole heaven passes to the saints of the Most High — an everlasting kingdom, all dominions serving Him. First principle: the end is not the beast's empire but the saints' inheritance under the Son of man.",
      "density": 2.175,
      "words": 39,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 21,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-7-10",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The Ancient of Days sits: thousand thousands minister, and the books open. First principle: heaven's courtroom precedes the kingdom — the record is read before the verdict and dominion are given to the Son.",
      "density": 2.1071,
      "words": 34,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-7-21",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The boastful horn prevails against the saints — for a time. First principle: the war against the saints is real, violent, and temporary; it is written so the suffering will not surprise us.",
      "density": 2.0821,
      "words": 33,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-2-35",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The image of empires falls to chaff while the stone fills the earth. First principle: human kingdoms are one statue; God's kingdom is a growing mountain — cut without hands, unstoppable in growth.",
      "density": 1.9679,
      "words": 33,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-7-13",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "One like a Son of Man comes with the clouds of heaven to the Ancient of Days. Jesus claims this title and this coming; Revelation repeats the cloud-coming. First principle: messianic authority is given and then revealed in glory.",
      "density": 1.9464,
      "words": 39,
      "sentences": 3,
      "maxSentenceWords": 17,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-8-11",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The daily sacrifice is taken away and the sanctuary cast down by the self-exalting power. First principle: the war against God wears a religious face — the desecration of worship is prophecy's center stage.",
      "density": 1.9357,
      "words": 34,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-2-45",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The interpretation is certain: God makes known what shall come hereafter. First principle: the kingdom is divine work — without hands — and the dream's certainty anchors faith against empire's confidence.",
      "density": 1.9179,
      "words": 31,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-8-17",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Gabriel lifts the fallen Daniel: the vision belongs to the time of the end. First principle: apocalyptic vision is for understanding, not entertainment — the appointed time makes sense of the symbols.",
      "density": 1.8286,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-2-34",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "A stone cut without hands smashes the statue and becomes a great mountain. First principle: God's kingdom is not a human empire; it arrives by divine act and fills the earth.",
      "density": 1.8036,
      "words": 31,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-2-44",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "In the days of those kings God sets up a kingdom that shall never be destroyed. Luke: of His kingdom there shall be no end. First principle: Christ's kingdom outlasts and absorbs all earthly thrones.",
      "density": 1.7893,
      "words": 35,
      "sentences": 3,
      "maxSentenceWords": 16,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-7-26",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The court sits; the persecutor's dominion is consumed unto the end. First principle: every blasphemous power has a scheduled end — the same judgment that vindicates saints removes beasts.",
      "density": 1.7536,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-7-14",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The Son of Man receives dominion, glory, and a kingdom that all peoples should serve Him. Matthew: all authority in heaven and earth. First principle: universal worship and rule belong to the Messiah.",
      "density": 1.7393,
      "words": 33,
      "sentences": 3,
      "maxSentenceWords": 16,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "dan-7-18",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The saints of the Most High possess the kingdom for ever. First principle: persecution's arc ends in possession — the little horn loses, the saints inherit.",
      "density": 1.5071,
      "words": 26,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 15,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
